PREAMBLE

Vain's C Portable Engine is free to use in any project, including commercial and closed-source games. In return,
improvements to the engine itself flow back to it, so that everyone who uses it benefits from what others fix.
This license keeps those two promises apart: the engine stays shared, and your own project stays yours.


1. DEFINITIONS

1.1  "Licensor" means surelynotvain, the copyright holder of the Engine.

1.2  "Engine" means Vain's C Portable Engine (VCPE), version 3.0 or later, as published by the Licensor at
     https://github.com/surelynotvain/vcpe or a successor location named there: its source code, runtime, tools,
     build files, tests and documentation, excluding Third-Party Material.

1.3  "Engine File" means any file of the Engine, and any file derived from one, whether modified, renamed,
     moved, split or merged into another file.

1.4  "Engine Change" means any of the following, in source form:
     (a) a modification of an Engine File;
     (b) a new file that extends or replaces Engine functionality rather than implementing Your Project, such as
         a new engine module, a replacement for an engine module, a converter tool for engine formats, or a fix
         or port of the Engine to another platform or toolchain.

1.5  "Your Project" means a game, application or other work that uses the Engine, excluding the Engine Files
     it contains. Your Project's own code, art, audio, text, levels and data are part of Your Project, however
     they are compiled, linked or packaged together with the Engine.

1.6  "Distribute" means to make a copy available to anyone other than You, in source or binary form, by any
     means, including publishing a download, an EBOOT, a disc or memory-stick image, or a hosted service.
     Sharing within a single legal entity, or with contractors working on Your behalf under confidentiality,
     is not Distribution.

1.7  "Contribution" means any work submitted to the Licensor for inclusion in the Engine, including under
     Section 4.

1.8  "Contributor" means the Licensor and every person or entity whose Contribution has been included in the
     Engine.

1.9  "Third-Party Material" means material in the Engine that is not owned by the Licensor or a Contributor,
     as listed in Section 9.

1.10 "You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this license.


