4. CONDITIONS

4.1  Contribute Engine Changes back.
     If You Distribute anything that contains or was built from an Engine Change, You must submit that Engine
     Change to the Licensor:
     (a) when: no later than 30 days after the first Distribution that contains it;
     (b) how: as a pull request to the Engine's repository, or, if a pull request is not possible for You, as a
         patch attached to an issue there or sent to the Licensor by another channel named in the repository;
     (c) what: the complete source of the Engine Change, in a form the Licensor can apply to the Engine version
         it is based on, with any build settings it needs and a short description of what it changes and how it
         was tested.
     The obligation is met once the submission is made, whether or not the Licensor accepts it. Engine Changes
     that You never Distribute carry no obligation. Submitting an Engine Change does not oblige You to publish
     it anywhere else.

4.2  Your Project stays Yours.
     Nothing in this license requires You to publish, disclose or license any part of Your Project. Linking,
     compiling or packaging Your Project together with the Engine, statically or otherwise, does not make
     Your Project an Engine Change.

4.3  Attribution.
     Your Project's credits, about screen, readme or accompanying documentation must state:
         "Uses Vain's C Portable Engine (VCPE) by surelynotvain."
     or an equivalent statement in the language of Your Project. If Your Project shows credits in game, the
     statement must appear there.

4.4  Notices.
     Copies of Engine Files in source form must keep this license, the copyright notice and any notices in
     those files. Modified Engine Files must carry a prominent statement that they were changed.

4.5  Names.
     This license grants no rights to the names "VCPE" or "Vain's C Portable Engine" or the Licensor's name,
     except for the attribution required by Section 4.3 and for describing Your Project truthfully as using
     the Engine. You may not imply that the Licensor endorses Your Project, or Distribute a modified Engine
     under the Engine's name without stating that it is modified.


5. CONTRIBUTIONS

5.1  License to the Licensor. By submitting a Contribution, You grant the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide,
     royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable license to use, modify, sublicense and relicense the
     Contribution, as part of the Engine or otherwise, and You grant every recipient of the Engine the
     licenses in Sections 2 and 3 for it.

5.2  Representations. By submitting a Contribution, You state that:
     (a) You have the right to submit it under this license;
     (b) it contains no material taken from a game, its data or its decompiled code, and no other material You
         are not allowed to license this way;
     (c) any part produced with the help of an AI system is disclosed as such in the submission, and You have
